{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.86,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C3"],
      "pins": ["C3.1", "C3.2"],
      "nets": ["+24V", "GND"],
      "observed": "C3 is connected between +24V and GND, but its value field and SPICE model say 100 µF while its footprint, library part, and description are for a 100 nF 0603 X7R ceramic capacitor.",
      "expected": "The component value, footprint, description, and simulation model should agree. A 0603 X7R part in this footprint is 100 nF; a 100 µF capacitor would require a different footprint and likely a different voltage/polarity implementation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C3\") (value \"100u\") (footprint \"Coert-Vonk:CAP X7R 100nF ±10 50V 0603 Murata\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(description \"0.1 µF ±10% 100V Ceramic Capacitor X7R 0603 (1608 Metric)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"3\") (name \"+24V\") ... (node (ref \"C3\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C3 0 +24V 100u"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The BOM/simulation request a 100 µF part while the physical footprint is a 100 nF 0603 ceramic. This can cause a sourcing/assembly mismatch or leave the board with far less decoupling than the simulated +24V rail, increasing noise and possible instability.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist and SPICE deck are largely consistent with the intended OPNhydro-r2 architecture, but C3 contains a clear internal mismatch: it is specified as 100 µF in the value/SPICE deck while its footprint and part description are a 100 nF 0603 ceramic capacitor."
}

